-- title:
--   Proposition 2 — with CVP, Var(p)_t ≥ c t^(α−1) for all t ≥ 2 (corrected range of c)
-- statement:
--   Let a price path $(p_t)$ follow Controlled Variance Pricing with $\alpha \in (0,1)$ and a constant $c$ satisfying, in addition to the policy's range,
--
--   $$0 < c \le 2^{-\alpha}(p_1 - p_2)^2 \min\{1/2, (3\alpha)^{-1}\}.$$
--
--   Then the sample variance of the prices satisfies
--
--   $$\operatorname{Var}(p)_t \ge c\, t^{\alpha - 1} \qquad \text{for all } t \ge 2.$$
--
--   The bound is deterministic: it holds along every path generated by the rule, whatever the demands. It is the exploration guarantee of CVP, and together with Lemma 1 it controls the smallest eigenvalue of the design matrix.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper states Proposition 2 for the policy's range $c < 2^{-\alpha}(p_1-p_2)^2\min\{1,(3\alpha)^{-1}\}$. Its proof (p. 781) uses $\operatorname{Var}(p)_2 = (p_1-p_2)^2/2$, but $\operatorname{Var}(p)_2 = (p_1-p_2)^2/4$, and the printed statement fails at $t = 2$: for $\alpha = 0.6$, $|p_1 - p_2| = 1$, $c = 0.35$ one gets $c\,2^{\alpha-1} \approx 0.265 > 0.25$. Replacing $1$ by $1/2$ inside the minimum restores the proof; the two ranges coincide for $\alpha \ge 2/3$.
-- source:
--   den Boer, Zwart, Simultaneously Learning and Optimizing Using Controlled Variance Pricing, Management Science 60(3):770–783 (2014), p. 776 (PDF 8), Proposition 2; proof p. 781 (PDF 13)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_KeskinZeevi_SufficientConditions_LeastSquares
import Definitions.Def_CVPricing_Regret_Model
import Definitions.Def_CVPricing_Regret_CVP

open KeskinZeevi.SufficientConditions

namespace CVPricing.Regret

/-- Proposition 2 (den Boer–Zwart 2014, p. 776), with the corrected range of `c`: along every price
path that follows CVP with `α ∈ (0, 1)` and `c ≤ 2^{−α}(p₁ − p₂)² min{1/2, (3α)⁻¹}`,
`Var(p)_t ≥ c t^{α−1}` for all `t ≥ 2`. The printed range `c < 2^{−α}(p₁ − p₂)² min{1, (3α)⁻¹}`
fails at `t = 2` (`Var(p)₂ = (p₁ − p₂)²/4`, not `/2` as printed in the proof, p. 781). -/
theorem sample_variance_lower_bound (M : Model) (α c : ℝ) (p d : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hp : IsCVPPath M α c p d)
    (hc : c ≤ (2 : ℝ) ^ (-α) * (p 1 - p 2) ^ 2 * min (1 / 2) (3 * α)⁻¹) :
    ∀ t : ℕ, 2 ≤ t → c * (t : ℝ) ^ (α - 1) ≤ sampleVar p t := by sorry

end CVPricing.Regret
